.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-CHAIN.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh \- stop the local server, reverse tunnel, EC2 Caddy and EC2 proxy instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-chain.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tears the chain down in five logged steps:
.IP 1. 4
Boot out the
.B org.mu2edaq.notify-server
launchd agent if loaded, run
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1),
and report anything still listening on 8095.
.B This stops the notification server itself:
no event from any path, including on\-network publishers and the OKD proxy,
is delivered until it is started again.
.IP 2. 4
Boot out the
.B org.mu2edaq.notify-proxy-tunnel
agent if loaded, stop the pid\-file tunnel, and report any stray SSH
connection to the instance.
.IP 3. 4
.B systemctl stop caddy
on the instance if it is running and reachable.
.IP 4. 4
Retract the public A record to the unroutable sink with
.B update-notify-dns.sh \-\-retract
when the instance's address is auto\-assigned and the record points at it, so
the name never dangles on a released address. A record that points elsewhere,
or an Elastic IP, is left alone.
.IP 5. 4
Stop the EC2 instance and wait for
.BR stopped .
.PP
Steps 1 to 3 continue past individual failures.
.SH OPTIONS
None; everything is set by environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.mu2edaq.notify-server.plist
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.mu2edaq.notify-proxy-tunnel.plist
launchd agents unloaded in steps 1 and 2 (macOS). Not kept in this
repository.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SERVER_LAUNCH_AGENT ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TUNNEL_LAUNCH_AGENT
Plist paths for the two agents.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_RETRACT
0 skips step 4.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_INSTANCE_ID ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_PIDFILE
As for
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DEBUG
1 enables
.BR "set \-x" .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when the instance reaches
.BR stopped ;
non\-zero when an AWS call in steps 3 to 5 fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scripts/stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-chain.sh
# bring the server back without the public edge:
launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id \-u) \e
    ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.mu2edaq.notify\-server.plist
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1)
.PP
.I docs/reverse-proxy-operations.md
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
.BR mu2edaq-phone-notification-system .
